  "memoryAboutInjectionBody": "At the start of a chat, the newest items of each type are placed in the model context. If a type exceeds the injection limit, the block is marked mode=\"summary\" with total and shown counts; the rest can be fetched with memory_search_profile. Raise the limit in Settings → Memory for more completeness at a higher token cost. In each assistant’s memory settings, select types to always inject in full.",
  "@memoryAboutInjectionBody": {
    "description": "Body text describing injection limits, the mode=\"summary\" marker with total/shown counts, memory_search_profile, and full-injection types."
  },
  "memoryAboutPipelineTitle": "Background pipeline",
  "@memoryAboutPipelineTitle": {
    "description": "Section heading in About memory describing the background auto-organize pipeline."
  },
  "memoryAboutPipelineBody": "Auto-organize runs after chats: decide whether anything is worth remembering, extract candidates, dedupe and merge, then distill identity items into the user profile when needed. You can also tap Organize on the assistant Memory tab. That is why the processing model is called often.",
  "@memoryAboutPipelineBody": {
    "description": "Body text describing the organize steps (decide, extract, dedupe/merge, distill) and why the model is called often."
  },
  "memoryAboutCacheTitle": "Keep caching healthy",
  "@memoryAboutCacheTitle": {
    "description": "Section heading in About memory about keeping prompt caching healthy."
  },
  "memoryAboutCacheBody": "The injected memory prefix is kept stable so unchanged chats can reuse the prompt cache, lowering cost and latency. Avoid pointless bulk edits or reshuffles. Day-to-day single-entry edits usually have limited impact.",
  "@memoryAboutCacheBody": {
    "description": "Body text advising a stable injected prefix to reuse prompt cache and avoid bulk edits that raise cost/latency."
  },
  "memoryAboutFaqTitle": "FAQ",
  "@memoryAboutFaqTitle": {
    "description": "Section heading in About memory for the FAQ; also used as the section title above FAQ entries."
  },
  "memoryAboutFaqWhyNotRememberedTitle": "Why wasn't this remembered?",
