  "scheduledTasksPreparationCost": "Preparation calls the model and may cost extra. With “Follow latest conversation”, new messages before the due time can invalidate a prepared result. Unused or cancelled output may still be billed, and preparing again makes another model request.",
  "@scheduledTasksPreparationCost": {
    "description": "Section footer warning that preparation calls the model and may incur charges, and that results can be invalidated or billed even if unused."
  },
  "scheduledTasksAllowPreparationTip": "Generate the next result before its scheduled time, while Cuplivo can run. The result stays out of the chat until it is due. Preparation uses text only, without tools, attachments or custom request bodies. It may incur model charges.",
  "@scheduledTasksAllowPreparationTip": {
    "description": "Tooltip on the advance preparation toggle explaining it generates results early, text-only, and may incur model charges."
  },
  "scheduledTasksContextPolicyTip": "Follow latest conversation: before the task is due, new messages, edits or switching message versions invalidate the prepared result; preparing again uses another attempt and may cost extra. Once due, the saved notification result is added to the chat unchanged.\n\nUse preparation snapshot: keep the prepared result even if the conversation changes. It will not reflect later messages.",
  "@scheduledTasksContextPolicyTip": {
    "description": "Long help text under the context-policy option in the scheduled task editor, explaining 'follow latest conversation' vs 'preparation snapshot' modes and their effect on prepared results and charges."
  },
  "scheduledTasksPreparationWindowTip": "How far ahead of the scheduled time preparation may begin, up to 24 hours. For example, opening Cuplivo at noon can prepare the next morning’s reminder. A larger window gives more chances to prepare, but the result may be less current. It does not change the scheduled time or guarantee background execution. Prepare now bypasses this automatic waiting period and all attempt limits.",
  "@scheduledTasksPreparationWindowTip": {
    "description": "Help tip for the preparation-window option (max 24h) in the scheduled task editor; explains how early preparation may start and that it neither changes the schedule nor guarantees background execution."
  },
  "scheduledTasksPreparationAttemptsTip": "Automatic preparation pauses when this occurrence reaches the total attempt limit. First attempts, failures, cancellations and manual preparation all count in the record. Prepare now can still run after this limit is reached. More attempts may incur more model charges; this is not a spending limit.",
  "@scheduledTasksPreparationAttemptsTip": {
    "description": "Help tip for the preparation attempt-limit option; explains that all attempts count, that Prepare now bypasses the limit, and that it is not a spending cap."
  },
  "scheduledTasksPreparationCooldownTip": "Minimum time between the start of preparation attempts for the same occurrence. Waiting longer reduces repeated requests. A retry still needs the app to be able to run; it is not a background timer. Prepare now bypasses this automatic waiting period and all attempt limits.",
  "@scheduledTasksPreparationCooldownTip": {
    "description": "Help tip for the preparation cooldown option; explains the minimum interval between preparation attempts and that retries need the app to run."
  },
  "scheduledTasksUnavailableTip": "If no prepared result is available and the task cannot run when due, send a reminder or skip the occurrence. A reminder contains no generated answer and requires notifications to be enabled. If Cuplivo is open when the task is due, it can run the task then.",
  "@scheduledTasksUnavailableTip": {
    "description": "Help tip for the unavailable-policy option; explains sending a reminder (no generated answer, needs notifications) or skipping when no prepared result exists and the task cannot run."
  },
  "scheduledTasksNotifyTip": "Allow result notifications and fallback reminders. Turning this off does not stop the task or model calls, and does not prevent preparation charges. System notification permission is also required.",
  "@scheduledTasksNotifyTip": {
    "description": "Help tip for the notification toggle; notes that disabling it does not stop task execution or model charges, and system permission is still required."
  },
  "scheduledTasksShowPreviewTip": "Show the prepared result text in the notification, including on the lock screen if allowed by system settings. Turn this off to show a generic notice; the full result remains available in the chat. Global notification privacy settings also apply.",
  "@scheduledTasksShowPreviewTip": {
    "description": "Help tip for the show-preview toggle; explains that the prepared result text appears in notifications (including lock screen) and that global privacy settings also apply."
  },
